# Modules

`Session` constructs match widgets and subscribes. It never grabs a child canvas or implements that widget's pointer machine.

`Session` exists only while a match is running, inside `PlayScreen`. `ScreenHost` shows exactly one `GameScreen`. Exit (confirm) replaces it.

```
app/      Canvas + rAF boot, ScreenHost. Creates Session on demand. Constructs Channel.
session/  One match: that map, input, widget subscriptions. Talks to Lockstep, never a socket.
sim/      Deterministic world. No Three.js, fetch, DOM, or net.
render/   Three.js drawing. Reads views, does not mutate sim.
ui/       DOM widgets and GameScreens. Own their DOM and input.
net/      Channel + lockstep mailbox. No Three.js, no rules, no World.tick.
tooling/  Separate Vite app (`npm run dev:tools`). May import render/sim. No Session, no net. World editor uses the game Renderer.
```

```ts
// BAD — session reaches into the widget
hud.minimap.addEventListener("pointerdown", ...)
paintMinimap(hud.minimap, view)

// GOOD
new Minimap(host, { onLookAt: (x, y) => session.lookAt(x, y) })
minimap.setView(view)
```
